% ============================================================================
% references.bib — multivac-paper
%
% Every entry below was VERIFIED ON THE WEB on 2026-09-02 against the arXiv API
% (export.arxiv.org/api/query), publisher pages, DBLP, PMLR, proceedings sites,
% GitHub raw files and the Hugging Face API. Nothing is from memory.
%
% Fields that could not be verified are marked with a "% UNVERIFIED:" comment on
% the line above them, or omitted entirely. Where a source publishes its own
% BibTeX, that form is used and the divergence from our house style is left
% alone deliberately.
%
% CONVENTIONS USED HERE
%   * arXiv preprint with no venue  -> @misc + eprint/archivePrefix/primaryClass,
%     doi = {10.48550/arXiv.XXXX.XXXXX} (arXiv mints one for every submission).
%   * arXiv preprint WITH a venue   -> @inproceedings with the venue, PLUS the
%     eprint fields, so the reader can reach the preprint. natbib/plain BibTeX
%     ignore unknown fields, biblatex renders them.
%   * Blog post / web page          -> @misc with howpublished + url + urldate.
%     (biblatex users: @online is equivalent and renders better.)
%   * Software / repository         -> @software. NOT supported by legacy BibTeX
%     styles (plain/unsrt/abbrv); those degrade it to @misc. If the target style
%     is plain BibTeX, change @software to @misc — the fields survive.
%   * Dataset                       -> @misc with a sha256 in `note`, because the
%     scores are only comparable against the same file.
%
% TEN of the entries below have NO publisher DOI, because arXiv preprints, PMLR
% proceedings, NeurIPS proceedings, ICLR proceedings and COLM do not mint them.
% For those the arXiv DOI is the only DOI that exists. Do not invent others.
%
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% STYLE COMPATIBILITY — read before choosing a .bst. Verified 2026-09-02 by
% reading the ENTRY declarations of the actual style files on CTAN.
%
%   style                     url  doi  eprint/archivePrefix/primaryClass  urldate
%   plain/unsrt/abbrv/alpha    -    -                 -                       -
%   plainnat/abbrvnat          Y    Y                 -                       -
%   IEEEtran                   Y    -                 -                       -
%   apsrev4-2 (REVTeX 4.2)     Y    Y                 Y                       -
%   biblatex + biber           Y    Y          Y (auto-mapped)                Y
%
% Consequences for THIS file:
%   * Under plain/unsrt/abbrv the `url` and `doi` fields are SILENTLY IGNORED
%     (plain.bst declares exactly 22 fields and drops the rest without warning).
%     If the target template uses one of those, move the URL into `howpublished`.
%     Most arXiv CS templates are natbib-based, which does carry url and doi.
%   * Under EVERY legacy style, @software emits
%       "Warning--entry type for ... isn't style-file defined"
%     and is then rendered through the `misc` driver — so it looks like it
%     worked while dropping `url` and `version`. If the template is plain
%     BibTeX, change every @software here to @misc; the fields survive because
%     the load-bearing content is already duplicated into `note`.
%   * `urldate` is biblatex-only and must be ISO yyyy-mm-dd — a non-ISO value
%     prints NO access date at all, silently. Legacy styles need
%     `note = {Accessed: YYYY-MM-DD}` instead. Several entries here carry both,
%     deliberately, so neither route loses it.
%   * biblatex maps `archivePrefix`->`eprinttype` and `primaryClass`->`eprintclass`
%     automatically (biblatex.def), and ships a dedicated `eprint:arxiv` renderer
%     that prints exactly arXiv's own `arXiv:2401.12345 [cs.CL]` form. arXiv's
%     native BibTeX export therefore works here unmodified.
%
% ARXIV DOIs ARE PER-PAPER, NOT PER-VERSION. `10.48550/arXiv.<id>` resolves;
% `...<id>v1` does NOT (verified: 404). Where a specific version matters, the
% `eprint` field with a `v#` suffix is the only identifier that carries it.
% Every entry below records the current version in a comment instead.
%
% AVOIDED THROUGHOUT: the Google-Scholar antipattern
%   @article{..., journal = {arXiv preprint arXiv:2505.09388}}
% which puts an identifier in a journal-title field, defeats every eprint-aware
% style, and cannot express a published version. Where a venue is confirmed,
% this file uses @inproceedings WITH the eprint fields, so both are reachable.
%
% Sources for the above: arXiv's own BibTeX endpoint https://arxiv.org/bibtex/<id>
% · https://info.arxiv.org/help/doi.html · https://info.arxiv.org/help/hypertex/index.html
% (note: the old /help/hypertex/bibstyles page is GONE — 404) ·
% https://mirrors.ctan.org/biblio/bibtex/base/plain.bst ·
% https://mirrors.ctan.org/macros/latex/contrib/natbib/plainnat.bst ·
% https://mirrors.ctan.org/macros/latex/contrib/biblatex/latex/biblatex.def ·
% https://mirrors.ctan.org/biblio/bibtex/base/btxdoc.tex
% For software specifically, biblatex-software (https://ctan.org/pkg/biblatex-software)
% gives real @software drivers plus native SWHID support, and is integrated into
% the ACM article style.
% ============================================================================


